## page_crud Tool - Page Management with Puck Visual Builder

The `page_crud` tool manages pages within Puck apps.

**Block Schema Reference:** `src/components/puck/blocks-schema.json` documents all blocks and system concepts.

### Methods
| Method | Description | Required Params |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| list | List pages in app | app_id |
| read | Get page by ID | page_id |
| create | Create page | app_id, data.name |
| update | Update page metadata | page_id, data |
| update_content | Update Puck content | page_id, data.templateData |
| publish | Make page public | page_id |
| unpublish | Make page private | page_id |
| delete | Delete page | page_id |

### Page Fields
- `id`: Unique page identifier
- `appId`: Parent app ID
- `name`: Display name
- `slug`: URL-friendly identifier
- `description`: What the page shows
- `order`: Position in navigation (number)
- `templateData`: **Puck visual content (JSON)** - see structure below
- `isPublic`: Whether page is published
- `requiresAuth`: Whether login is required
- `allowedRoles`: Array of role names for access control

### Puck templateData Structure

```json
{
  "root": { "props": { "title": "Page Title" } },
  "content": [
    { "type": "BlockName", "props": { ... } }
  ],
  "zones": {}
}
```

